WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.798
Build a small evaluation set from the intended workload.

00:00:03.798 --> 00:00:08.318
Include common prompts, difficult edge cases, required formats, representative context lengths,

00:00:08.318 --> 00:00:10.372
and tasks with verifiable outcomes.

00:00:10.372 --> 00:00:14.070
Keep the base model, runtime, prompt template, sampling settings,

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.947
and hardware constant while comparing quantization variants.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:21.055
Otherwise, the test cannot isolate precision as the changed variable.

00:00:21.055 --> 00:00:25.164
Compare at least one compact candidate, one practical middle candidate,

00:00:25.164 --> 00:00:28.041
and a higher-precision reference when hardware allows.

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:33.793
Measure file size, loaded VRAM or RAM, model load time, time to first token,

00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:38.313
prompt-processing speed, generation speed, power or temperature if relevant, and errors.

00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:44.065
Run multiple trials so warm caches and random output do not determine the result.

00:00:44.065 --> 00:00:46.120
Score quality against predefined criteria.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.763
For coding, run tests.

00:00:47.763 --> 00:00:49.407
For extraction, compare fields.

00:00:49.407 --> 00:00:51.872
For structured output, validate the format.

00:00:51.872 --> 00:00:54.338
For analysis, review correctness and consistency.

00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:58.858
Long-context evaluation should use material that requires retrieval from different positions.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.323
Record failures, not only average impressions,

00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:05.843
because one serious instruction-following defect may outweigh a small speed gain.

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:11.184
Keep a concise decision log with model revision, quantization file, runtime version, settings,

00:01:11.184 --> 00:01:13.239
hardware, measurements, and acceptance result.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:18.580
Select the lowest-resource option that meets quality and reliability requirements with memory headroom.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.100
Revisit the decision when the model, runtime, hardware, or workload changes.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.620
Testing turns quantization from a label into an evidence-based deployment choice.
